### RFC 9457 Problem Details (replaces RFC 7807) — one error shape for every endpoint
HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request
Content-Type: application/problem+json

{
  "type": "https://api.example.com/problems/validation",
  "title": "Request validation failed",
  "status": 400,
  "detail": "2 fields are invalid",
  "instance": "/v1/orders",
  "traceId": "4bf92f3577b34da6",
  "errors": [
    { "field": "customerId", "message": "must not be blank" },
    { "field": "items[0].quantity", "message": "must be greater than 0" }
  ]
}

### Rate limited: tell the client when to come back
HTTP/1.1 429 Too Many Requests
Retry-After: 30
Content-Type: application/problem+json

{ "type": "https://api.example.com/problems/rate-limit", "title": "Too many requests", "status": 429 }
